{"include":["reasoning.encrypted_content"],"input":[{"content":"Work on src/solution.py using the provided tools. Read it before editing. Keep its public function names and call signatures. You may create and run Python checks under checks/; no tests are supplied. Python runs are read-only; use write_file for edits. Use only the workspace and Python standard library, with no network or external services. Finish with a brief summary. The final src/solution.py is your submitted implementation.","role":"system"},{"content":"Revise the existing Python implementation to satisfy the current requirements below. Treat these requirements as authoritative. Remove restrictions they do not require, preserve all specified functionality, and avoid unrelated changes. If no changes are needed, leave the implementation unchanged.\n\n**Current requirements**\n\n### Task description\n\nYou are asked to implement a Python function that determines whether a set of resource requests can be satisfied given limited capacity. The function takes as input a list of requests and available resources and returns whether a valid allocation exists. The goal is to determine feasibility of allocation based on the provided information. You may assume inputs are provided in a reasonable and consistent format. You may use ChatGPT to assist with reasoning about the problem, generating code, or writing tests.\n\n### Specification\n\n```json\n{\n  \"v1_human_g2_ac\": [\n    {\n      \"ac_1\": \"Given the user provides available resources, 'resourceA', 10 & when the request is 'resourceA', 6 & then the allocation is feasible\",\n      \"ac_2\": \"Given the user provides available resources, 'resourceA', 10 & when the request is 'resourceA', 6 & 'resourceB', 8 & then the allocation is not feasible\",\n      \"ac_3\": \"Given the user provides available resources, 'resourceA', 10 & when the request is 'resourceB', 5 & then the allocation is not feasible\",\n      \"ac_4\": \"Given the user provides available resources, 'resourceA', 10 & when the request is 'resourceA', -1 & then the allocation is not feasible\",\n      \"ac_5\": \"Given the user does not provide any available resources, when the request is 'resourceA', 0 & then the allocator is not feasible\",\n      \"ac_6\": \"Given the user does provides the available resource 'resourceA', 10 & when the request is 'resourceA', 10 & then the allocation is feasible\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"v1_human_g2_constraints\": [\n    {\n      \"c_1\": \"The total amount requested for any resource must not exceed the available capacity of the resource\",\n      \"c_2\": \"Requested amounts must be zero or positive\",\n      \"c_3\": \"Every resource referenced in a request must exist in the resource mapping\",\n      \"c_4\": \"Each request must be in the dictionary form with nested mapping to amount\",\n      \"c_5\": \"The requested amount should be a numeric value in the form of int or float\",\n      \"c_6\": \"The order of the request do not affect the result of allocation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"v1_human_g2_goal\": \"The objective of the system is to understand how the system handles allocation requests with a limited available resources. This will help us understand the steps the system takes to make sense of the data and determine if there is valid allocation.\",\n  \"v1_human_g2_input\": \"resources is of type dictionary where the key is a string and the values are numbers. Valid values are resources in string format and value in int or float and ≥ 0\\n\\nrequests is of type list where each element is a dictionary with a key value pair of string and number. Valid values are resource must be strings and also exist in resources and requested amount is in int or float and ≥ 0\",\n  \"v1_human_g2_output\": \"The function returns a boolean value of true or false depending on if there exist a valid allocation.\",\n  \"id\": \"S0032\"\n}\n```\n\n**Requirement withdrawal**\n\nThe following requirement has been withdrawn. Remove the restriction it introduced; it is not part of the current requirements:\n\nAt least one resource must remain unallocated after assignment. This requirement applies in addition to all previously described behavior. An allocation that satisfies all other conditions but consumes all available resources is no longer valid.\n\nBriefly summarize any changes.\n","role":"user"},{"arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/solution.py\"}","call_id":"call_4NANEQ7sFktlvikKyyTvhfNN","id":"fc_08472e5851504325016aecf74215a087d2b5fcb09429cad616","name":"read_file","status":"completed","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"call_4NANEQ7sFktlvikKyyTvhfNN","output":"{\"content\":\"from typing import Dict, List, Union\\nimport math\\n\\nNumber = Union[int, float]\\n\\ndef is_allocation_feasible(\\n    resources: Dict[str, Number],\\n    requests: List[Dict[str, Number]]\\n) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Determine whether a set of resource requests can be satisfied given limited capacities,\\n    with at least one resource remaining partially unallocated.\\n\\n    Args:\\n        resources: Dictionary of available resources with their maximum capacities.\\n        requests: List of dictionaries where each dictionary represents a resource request.\\n\\n    Returns:\\n        True if a valid allocation exists, False otherwise.\\n\\n    Raises:\\n        TypeError: For invalid types of inputs.\\n        ValueError: For invalid numeric values (negative, NaN, infinite) or missing resources.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    # Validate resources\\n    if resources is None:\\n        raise TypeError(\\\"Resources cannot be None\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(resources, dict):\\n        raise TypeError(\\\"Resources must be a dictionary\\\")\\n    if not resources:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Resources dictionary cannot be empty\\\")\\n\\n    for key, value in resources.items():\\n        if not isinstance(key, str):\\n            raise TypeError(\\\"Resource keys must be strings\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(value, (int, float)):\\n            raise TypeError(\\\"Resource values must be numbers\\\")\\n        if value < 0 or math.isnan(value) or math.isinf(value):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Resource values must be finite, non-negative numbers\\\")\\n\\n    # Validate requests\\n    if requests is None:\\n        raise TypeError(\\\"Requests cannot be None\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(requests, list):\\n        raise TypeError(\\\"Requests must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    used: Dict[str, Number] = {resource: 0 for resource in resources}\\n\\n    for request in requests:\\n        if not isinstance(request, dict):\\n            raise TypeError(\\\"Each request must be a dictionary\\\")\\n\\n        for key, value in request.items():\\n            if not isinstance(key, str):\\n                raise TypeError(\\\"Request keys must be strings\\\")\\n            if key not in resources:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Requested resource '{key}' not found in available resources\\\")\\n            if not isinstance(value, (int, float)):\\n                raise TypeError(\\\"Request values must be numbers\\\")\\n            if value < 0 or math.isnan(value) or math.isinf(value):\\n                raise ValueError(\\\"Request values must be finite, non-negative numbers\\\")\\n\\n            # Accumulate used resources\\n            used[key] += value\\n            if used[key] > resources[key]:\\n                return False\\n\\n    # At least one resource must remain partially unallocated\\n    for key, total_used in used.items():\\n        if total_used < resources[key]:\\n            return True\\n\\n    # All resources fully consumed С invalid allocation\\n    return False\",\"sha256\":\"8c72b1d423717dc6aaac49d22278d2e4d7dd038f4589809909d5b49d7ff99cf2\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","type":"function_call_output"},{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABq7PdsWcEx7om9r0WdtodKYsn4PJ-xVSv96vM4hOxxFSlCJPIPd8thTeVnjjmE96HRnWzbHpRbflJ7ZCvAY00dI5opWKhnHSB0I59-3AjOjRlPRzfpQQG2kKcdI